# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` must NOT upload from backend/.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, because its absence is not obvious and the failure is silent:
# gcloud tars up the current directory and uploads it to the Cloud Build staging
# bucket BEFORE Docker ever runs. It looks for an ignore file in the directory it is
# uploading and does NOT walk up to a parent's .gitignore, so the repo-root
# Chirp/.gitignore -- which does list .env -- has no effect here. With no file at
# this path, `gcloud meta list-files-for-upload` run from backend/ lists `.env`
# literally, alongside the whole .venv/ and tests/ trees.
#
# The container image was never the problem: backend/Dockerfile uses explicit COPY
# statements (pyproject.toml, alembic.ini, alembic/, app/) rather than `COPY . .`,
# so .env cannot reach the image. But that protection only applies AFTER Cloud Build
# already holds the raw source archive, in cleartext, in GCS. .env carries a live
# RESEND_API_KEY and the Stripe keys.
#
# If you add a build step that needs one of these paths, remove that line rather
# than deleting the file.

# Secrets. The whole reason this file exists.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*-service-account*.json

# The virtualenv: thousands of files, none of them used by the image build.
.venv/
venv/

# Test and build artifacts the Dockerfile does not COPY.
tests/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
htmlcov/
.coverage
